<</Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/Alt (Three stacked panels plotting vaccine efficacy against measured neutralising antibody level, with 95% confidence intervals: an mRNA vaccine rising from 78% to 96% efficacy across a hundredfold antibody range, a protein-subunit vaccine showing the same rise, and a vector vaccine in which severe disease is still 63% prevented at antibody levels below the assay limit while moderate disease is only 33% prevented. A glossary band defines every term.)
